# cross-desk-limit — always read the source of truth first

Before changing anything in this project, read:

1. `REQUIREMENTS.md` — sections §1 through §12 of the operator's brief, verbatim.
2. `docs/PLAN.md` — the complete brief, verbatim, including the milestones (§17),
   the unconfirmed items (§20), what is out of scope (§21), the test list (§22) and
   the acceptance checks (§23).

Those two files are the only source of truth. Do not clone, read or depend on any
other repository.

## Rules that always apply

- Rules and values marked **PROVISIONAL** are not confirmed by the owning team and
  may change. A provisional rule stays as one small function or one constant the
  operator can edit — do not build abstraction layers around it "just in case".
- Confidentiality: never write the employer's name, an internal hostname, URL,
  library/schema name, credential, or a real counterparty or limit value into any
  file, commit message or log line. Use `<LIBRARY>`, `<URL>`, `ABCD` / `ABCDEFG`
  style placeholders. Environment-specific values live in gitignored config.
- `pandas` may be imported only inside `src/cdl/treats/` and in
  `prototype/check_limit.py`.
- `prototype/check_limit.py` imports nothing from `src/`; it must stay readable
  top to bottom.
- Dependency direction: `ui` and `cli` may import `logic` and `store`; `logic` may
  import `treats` and `constants`; nothing imports `ui`.
- Forbidden anywhere: FastAPI, Streamlit, SQLAlchemy, pydantic, any HTTP server,
  any background scheduler.
- Type-annotate public functions. English UI only.
- Keep the parity between the standalone prototype and the package: the parity
  test in §22 must stay green.
